[{"id":"wa","jp":"〜は","meaning":"提示主题，相当于“至于……/……是……”","meaningEn":"as for; marks the topic of the sentence","rule":"名词 + は","notes":"Written は but pronounced 'wa'. It sets up what the sentence is about; the key information comes after it.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"私は学生です。","en":"I am a student.","cn":"我是一名学生。"},{"ja":"今日は天気がいいです。","en":"The weather is nice today.","cn":"今天天气很好。"},{"ja":"この本はおもしろいです。","en":"This book is interesting.","cn":"这本书很有趣。"}]},{"id":"ga-subject","jp":"〜が（主语）","meaning":"标记主语；强调新信息或焦点","meaningEn":"marks the subject; points out new or focused information","rule":"名词 + が","notes":"Question words such as だれ and 何 take が, never は, when they are the subject. が is also used with 好き, ほしい, 上手 and わかる for the thing liked, wanted or understood.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"雨が降っています。","en":"It is raining.","cn":"下雨了。"},{"ja":"だれが窓を開けましたか。","en":"Who opened the window?","cn":"谁开的窗户？"},{"ja":"私が行きます。","en":"I'll be the one to go.","cn":"我会去的。"}]},{"id":"o","jp":"〜を","meaning":"标记动作对象；也可标记经过或离开的地点","meaningEn":"marks the direct object of a verb; marks a place moved through or left","rule":"名词 + を","notes":"Written を but pronounced 'o'. With movement verbs such as 歩く, 散歩する and 出る it marks the route or the place being left.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"毎朝パンを食べます。","en":"I eat bread every morning.","cn":"我每天早上都吃面包。"},{"ja":"姉は新しいかばんを買いました。","en":"My older sister bought a new bag.","cn":"我姐姐买了一个新包。"},{"ja":"公園を散歩しました。","en":"I took a walk in the park.","cn":"我在公园里散步。"}]},{"id":"ni-time","jp":"〜に（时间）","meaning":"表示具体时间点的“在……”","meaningEn":"at; on; in (a specific point in time)","rule":"名词 + に","notes":"Used with clock times, dates, days of the week and months. Relative words such as 今日, 明日, 毎日 and 来週 take no に.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"毎朝7時に起きます。","en":"I get up at seven every morning.","cn":"我每天早上7点起床。"},{"ja":"日曜日に友達と会います。","en":"I'm meeting a friend on Sunday.","cn":"我周日要去见我的朋友们。"},{"ja":"8月に国へ帰ります。","en":"I'm going back to my country in August.","cn":"我将于8月返回该国。"}]},{"id":"ni-destination","jp":"〜に（目的地）","meaning":"表示移动的目的地“到……”","meaningEn":"to; into (the destination of movement)","rule":"名词 + に + 行く / 来る / 帰る","notes":"Close in meaning to へ. に puts the focus on the arrival point, へ on the direction.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"毎日バスで学校に行きます。","en":"I go to school by bus every day.","cn":"我每天乘公共汽车去上学。"},{"ja":"夜10時に家に帰りました。","en":"I got home at 10 p.m.","cn":"我晚上10点回家。"},{"ja":"来月、姉が日本に来ます。","en":"My older sister is coming to Japan next month.","cn":"我姐姐下个月要来日本。"}]},{"id":"ni-location","jp":"〜に（存在地点）","meaning":"表示人或物存在的位置“在……”","meaningEn":"in; at; on (where someone or something is)","rule":"名词 + に + ある / いる","notes":"Used with ある, いる and 住む. For the place where an action happens (eat, study, play), use で instead.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"机の上に辞書があります。","en":"There is a dictionary on the desk.","cn":"书桌上有一本字典。"},{"ja":"姉は東京に住んでいます。","en":"My older sister lives in Tokyo.","cn":"我姐姐住在东京。"},{"ja":"猫は今どこにいますか。","en":"Where is the cat now?","cn":"猫现在在哪里？"}]},{"id":"ni-indirect-object","jp":"〜に（间接宾语）","meaning":"表示动作的对象或接受者“给……”","meaningEn":"to (the person who receives or is the target of an action)","rule":"名词 + に","notes":"Common with あげる, 貸す, 教える, 見せる, 電話をかける and 会う. With もらう and 借りる, に marks the person you get something from.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"母に手紙を書きます。","en":"I'm going to write a letter to my mother.","cn":"给我妈妈写封信。"},{"ja":"妹に本を貸しました。","en":"I lent a book to my younger sister.","cn":"我借给妹妹一本书。"},{"ja":"友達に電話をかけました。","en":"I called my friend.","cn":"我打电话给我的朋友。"}]},{"id":"ni-frequency","jp":"〜に（频率）","meaning":"表示频率单位，相当于“每……”","meaningEn":"per; in (how many times within a period)","rule":"名词 + に + 名词","notes":"The period comes first, then に, then the number of times: 月に一回 (once a month).","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"一週間に二回、プールで泳ぎます。","en":"I swim in the pool twice a week.","cn":"每周两次在泳池中游泳。"},{"ja":"母は一日に二回、犬の散歩をします。","en":"My mother walks the dog twice a day.","cn":"我妈妈每天遛狗两次。"},{"ja":"一年に一度、家族で旅行します。","en":"Once a year, my family goes on a trip.","cn":"我每年和家人一起旅行一次。"}]},{"id":"e","jp":"〜へ","meaning":"表示移动方向“向／往……”","meaningEn":"to; toward (the direction of movement)","rule":"名词 + へ","notes":"Written へ but pronounced 'e'. Usually interchangeable with に for destinations; へ stresses the direction a little more.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"夏休みに北海道へ行きます。","en":"I'm going to Hokkaido during summer vacation.","cn":"我要去北海道度暑假。"},{"ja":"来週、国へ帰ります。","en":"I'm going back to my home country next week.","cn":"我下周要回国。"},{"ja":"どこへ行きますか。","en":"Where are you going?","cn":"你要去哪里？"}]},{"id":"de-place","jp":"〜で（动作地点）","meaning":"表示动作发生的场所“在……”","meaningEn":"at; in (the place where an action happens)","rule":"名词 + で","notes":"Compare 教室にいます (being somewhere: に) with 教室で勉強します (doing something there: で).","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"図書館で本を読みます。","en":"I read books at the library.","cn":"在图书馆里读一本书。"},{"ja":"きのう、デパートでくつを買いました。","en":"Yesterday I bought shoes at the department store.","cn":"昨天，我在一家百货公司买了一双鞋。"},{"ja":"駅の前で友達を待ちました。","en":"I waited for my friend in front of the station.","cn":"我在车站前等我的朋友。"}]},{"id":"de-means","jp":"〜で（手段）","meaning":"表示手段、工具、方法或语言“用／通过……”","meaningEn":"by; with; in (means, tool, method or language)","rule":"名词 + で","notes":"To say 'on foot', use 歩いて行きます rather than で.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"毎日電車で会社へ行きます。","en":"I go to work by train every day.","cn":"我每天乘火车上班。"},{"ja":"はしでご飯を食べます。","en":"I eat my meals with chopsticks.","cn":"我用筷子吃饭。"},{"ja":"日本語で手紙を書きました。","en":"I wrote a letter in Japanese.","cn":"我用日语写了一封信。"}]},{"id":"to-and","jp":"〜と（并列）","meaning":"连接名词列举全部项目“和……”","meaningEn":"and (joining nouns in a complete list)","rule":"名词 + と + 名词","notes":"と lists every item; to give just some examples, use や. It joins nouns only, not verbs or adjectives.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"かばんの中にペンとノートがあります。","en":"There is a pen and a notebook in my bag.","cn":"包里有一支笔和笔记本。"},{"ja":"朝ご飯にパンとたまごを食べました。","en":"I had bread and eggs for breakfast.","cn":"我早餐吃了面包和鸡蛋。"},{"ja":"父と母は銀行で働いています。","en":"My father and mother work at a bank.","cn":"我的父亲和母亲在银行工作。"}]},{"id":"to-with","jp":"〜と（共同）","meaning":"表示共同动作的伙伴“和……一起”","meaningEn":"with; together with (a partner in an action)","rule":"名词 + と","notes":"Often followed by いっしょに. With verbs like 話す, 会う and 結婚する, と marks the other person.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"週末、友達と映画を見ました。","en":"I saw a movie with a friend on the weekend.","cn":"周末我和朋友看了一部电影。"},{"ja":"妹といっしょに買い物に行きます。","en":"I'm going shopping with my younger sister.","cn":"我和妹妹一起去购物。"},{"ja":"だれと昼ご飯を食べましたか。","en":"Who did you have lunch with?","cn":"您和谁共进午餐？"}]},{"id":"ya","jp":"〜や","meaning":"列举部分项目“……呀……等等”","meaningEn":"and (giving some examples out of more); ... and so on","rule":"名词 + や + 名词","notes":"Suggests the list is not complete. Often ends with など: 本や雑誌など.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"机の上に本や雑誌があります。","en":"On the desk there are books, magazines and so on.","cn":"书桌上有书籍和杂志。"},{"ja":"スーパーで肉や野菜を買いました。","en":"I bought meat, vegetables and other things at the supermarket.","cn":"我在超市买了肉和蔬菜。"}]},{"id":"ka-or","jp":"〜か（选择）","meaning":"在名词选项间表示“或者”","meaningEn":"or (a choice between nouns)","rule":"名词 + か + 名词","notes":"Means one of the items is chosen. To list items together, use と or や.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"飲み物はコーヒーか紅茶がいいです。","en":"For a drink, coffee or tea would be good.","cn":"我更喜欢咖啡或茶。"},{"ja":"土曜日か日曜日に買い物に行きます。","en":"I'll go shopping on Saturday or Sunday.","cn":"我周六或周日去购物。"},{"ja":"駅までバスかタクシーで行きます。","en":"I'll go to the station by bus or taxi.","cn":"乘坐巴士或出租车前往车站。"}]},{"id":"mo","jp":"〜も","meaning":"表示“也”；用于否定时表示“也不”","meaningEn":"also; too; (with a negative) not ... either; neither ... nor","rule":"名词 + も","notes":"も replaces は, が and を, but comes after other particles: 京都にも行きました.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"私も学生です。","en":"I'm a student too.","cn":"我也是一名学生。"},{"ja":"兄はサッカーも好きです。","en":"My older brother likes soccer too.","cn":"我哥哥也喜欢足球。"},{"ja":"肉も魚も食べません。","en":"I eat neither meat nor fish.","cn":"我不吃肉或鱼。"}]},{"id":"no","jp":"〜の（所属）","meaning":"表示所属、归属或修饰关系“的”","meaningEn":"'s; of (possession, belonging or description)","rule":"名词 + の + 名词","notes":"The first noun describes the second: 日本の車 (a Japanese car). The second noun can be dropped when clear: それは私のです.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"これは私のかさです。","en":"This is my umbrella.","cn":"这是我的雨伞。"},{"ja":"日本語の先生はとてもやさしいです。","en":"The Japanese teacher is very kind.","cn":"日语老师非常友善。"},{"ja":"駅の近くに新しい店があります。","en":"There is a new shop near the station.","cn":"车站附近有一家新商店。"}]},{"id":"kara-from","jp":"〜から（起点）","meaning":"表示起点“从……”","meaningEn":"from (a starting point in time or place)","rule":"名词 + から","notes":"Often paired with まで: 月曜日から金曜日まで (from Monday to Friday).","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"授業は9時からです。","en":"Class starts at nine.","cn":"9点开始上课。"},{"ja":"学校から駅まで歩きます。","en":"I walk from school to the station.","cn":"从学校步行到车站。"},{"ja":"私はブラジルから来ました。","en":"I'm from Brazil.","cn":"我来自巴西。"}]},{"id":"made","jp":"〜まで（终点）","meaning":"表示终点“到……为止”","meaningEn":"until; up to; as far as","rule":"名词 + まで","notes":"Marks the end point of something that continues. For a deadline ('by'), use までに (N4).","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"昼休みは1時までです。","en":"Lunch break is until one o'clock.","cn":"午餐休息时间为1点前。"},{"ja":"駅までいっしょに行きましょう。","en":"Let's go together as far as the station.","cn":"我们一起去车站吧。"},{"ja":"きのうは夜11時まで勉強しました。","en":"Yesterday I studied until 11 p.m.","cn":"昨天，我学习到晚上11点。"}]},{"id":"ka-question","jp":"〜か（疑问）","meaning":"句末疑问助词“吗”","meaningEn":"(question marker) turns a sentence into a question","rule":"句子 + か","notes":"Polite questions end in か and are usually written with 。. In casual speech か is normally dropped and rising intonation is used instead.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"これはあなたのかばんですか。","en":"Is this your bag?","cn":"这是你的包吗？"},{"ja":"朝ご飯を食べましたか。","en":"Did you eat breakfast?","cn":"您吃过早餐吗？"},{"ja":"トイレはどこですか。","en":"Where is the restroom?","cn":"厕所在哪里？"}]},{"id":"ne","jp":"〜ね","meaning":"征求认同或共鸣“呢／对吧”","meaningEn":"isn't it?; right? (seeking agreement or sharing a feeling)","rule":"句子 + ね","notes":"Used when the speaker expects the listener to share the same view or knowledge. Compare よ, which tells the listener something new.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"今日は暑いですね。","en":"It's hot today, isn't it?","cn":"今天很热，不是吗？"},{"ja":"このケーキ、おいしいですね。","en":"This cake is delicious, isn't it?","cn":"这个蛋糕很好吃。"},{"ja":"明日のテストは10時からですね。","en":"Tomorrow's test starts at ten, right?","cn":"明天的测试是从10点开始的。"}]},{"id":"yo","jp":"〜よ","meaning":"提示新信息或加强语气“哦／呀”","meaningEn":"you know; I tell you (giving new information or emphasis)","rule":"句子 + よ","notes":"Tells the listener something they may not know. Overusing it with superiors can sound pushy.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"このラーメンはとてもおいしいですよ。","en":"This ramen is really good, you know.","cn":"这道拉面非常美味。"},{"ja":"かさを忘れていますよ。","en":"You're forgetting your umbrella.","cn":"我忘带雨伞了。"},{"ja":"明日はテストがありますよ。","en":"There's a test tomorrow, you know.","cn":"我们明天有一个测试。"}]},{"id":"yori","jp":"〜より","meaning":"比较基准“比……”","meaningEn":"than (the standard of comparison)","rule":"名词 + より","notes":"In X は Y より + adjective, Y is the standard. Japanese adjectives have no '-er' form; より does that job.","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"今日はきのうより寒いです。","en":"Today is colder than yesterday.","cn":"今天比昨天冷。"},{"ja":"電車はバスより速いです。","en":"Trains are faster than buses.","cn":"火车比巴士快。"},{"ja":"兄は父より背が高いです。","en":"My older brother is taller than my father.","cn":"我弟弟比我父亲高。"}]},{"id":"no-hou-ga-yori","jp":"〜の方が〜より","meaning":"比较两者：A比B更……","meaningEn":"X is more ... than Y","rule":"名词 + の方が + 名词 + より","notes":"The two parts can come in either order. Often used to answer a どちら question.","group":"比较","examples":[{"ja":"犬の方が猫より好きです。","en":"I like dogs more than cats.","cn":"与猫相比，我更喜欢狗。"},{"ja":"東京の方が大阪より人が多いです。","en":"Tokyo has more people than Osaka.","cn":"东京的人口比大阪还多。"},{"ja":"夏より冬の方が好きです。","en":"I like winter better than summer.","cn":"与夏天相比，我更喜欢冬天。"}]},{"id":"to-to-dochira-ga","jp":"〜と〜とどちらが","meaning":"询问两者中哪一个更……","meaningEn":"which is more ..., X or Y?","rule":"名词 + と + 名词 + とどちらが","notes":"Compares exactly two things. どっち is the casual form of どちら. Answer with 〜の方が.","group":"比较","examples":[{"ja":"コーヒーと紅茶とどちらが好きですか。","en":"Which do you like better, coffee or tea?","cn":"您更喜欢咖啡还是茶？"},{"ja":"電車とバスとどちらが安いですか。","en":"Which is cheaper, the train or the bus?","cn":"火车和公共汽车哪个更便宜？"},{"ja":"「山と海とどちらがいいですか。」「海の方がいいです。」","en":"\"Which is better, the mountains or the sea?\" \"The sea is better.\"","cn":"“山还是海，哪个更好？”“大海更好。”"}]},{"id":"no-naka-de-ga-ichiban","jp":"〜の中で〜が一番","meaning":"在范围中表示“最……”","meaningEn":"... is the most ... among/of","rule":"名词 + の中で + 名词 + が一番","notes":"Used for three or more items. In questions use 何, だれ, どこ or いつ before が一番.","group":"比较","examples":[{"ja":"果物の中でりんごが一番好きです。","en":"Of all fruits, I like apples the most.","cn":"我最喜欢苹果，最喜欢水果。"},{"ja":"クラスの中でだれが一番背が高いですか。","en":"Who is the tallest in the class?","cn":"谁是班上最高的人？"},{"ja":"家族の中で父が一番早く起きます。","en":"In my family, my father gets up the earliest.","cn":"我父亲在家里醒得最早。"}]},{"id":"desu","jp":"〜です","meaning":"礼貌判断句的系词“是……”","meaningEn":"is; am; are (polite copula)","rule":"名词 + です / な形容词 + です / い形容词 + です","notes":"Forms: です, ではありません, でした, ではありませんでした. After an い-adjective, です only adds politeness: 高いです.","group":"判断句","examples":[{"ja":"私はマリアです。","en":"I'm Maria.","cn":"我叫Maria。"},{"ja":"今日は月曜日です。","en":"Today is Monday.","cn":"今天是星期一。"},{"ja":"この部屋はとても静かです。","en":"This room is very quiet.","cn":"这个房间非常安静。"}]},{"id":"da","jp":"〜だ","meaning":"普通体判断句“是……”","meaningEn":"is; am; are (plain copula)","rule":"名词 + だ / な形容词 + だ","notes":"Forms: だ, じゃない, だった, じゃなかった. Never used right after an い-adjective (高いだ is wrong). Often dropped in casual questions: 学生？","group":"判断句","examples":[{"ja":"今日は日曜日だ。","en":"Today is Sunday.","cn":"今天是星期天。"},{"ja":"あの人は私の兄だ。","en":"That person is my older brother.","cn":"他是我弟弟。"},{"ja":"明日は休みだから、ゆっくり寝る。","en":"Tomorrow is a day off, so I'll sleep in.","cn":"明天是休息日，所以我会慢慢睡觉。"}]},{"id":"de-wa-arimasen-ja-nai","jp":"〜ではありません / 〜じゃない","meaning":"礼貌或普通体否定判断“不是……”","meaningEn":"is not; am not; are not","rule":"名词 + ではありません / な形容词 + ではありません / 名词 + じゃない / な形容词 + じゃない","notes":"じゃありません and じゃないです are more conversational polite forms. Past: ではありませんでした / じゃなかった. い-adjectives use 〜くない instead.","group":"判断句","examples":[{"ja":"私は先生ではありません。学生です。","en":"I'm not a teacher. I'm a student.","cn":"我不是老师。我是一名学生。"},{"ja":"今日は休みじゃない。","en":"Today isn't a day off.","cn":"我不会休息一天。"},{"ja":"この町はあまりにぎやかではありません。","en":"This town isn't very lively.","cn":"这个城镇不能太繁忙。"}]},{"id":"deshita","jp":"〜でした","meaning":"礼貌体过去判断“曾是／当时是……”","meaningEn":"was; were (polite past copula)","rule":"名词 + でした / な形容词 + でした","notes":"Past negative: ではありませんでした. い-adjectives do not take でした: say 高かったです, not 高いでした.","group":"判断句","examples":[{"ja":"きのうは私の誕生日でした。","en":"Yesterday was my birthday.","cn":"昨天是我的生日。"},{"ja":"子どものころ、野菜がきらいでした。","en":"When I was a child, I didn't like vegetables.","cn":"小时候，我不喜欢吃蔬菜。"},{"ja":"テストはかんたんでした。","en":"The test was easy.","cn":"测试很简单。"}]},{"id":"masu","jp":"〜ます","meaning":"礼貌体非过去动词（做／将做）","meaningEn":"polite non-past verb ending (do; will do)","rule":"动词ます形词干 + ます","notes":"Covers habits and future actions. 飲む→飲みます, 食べる→食べます, する→します, 来る→来ます.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"毎朝コーヒーを飲みます。","en":"I drink coffee every morning.","cn":"我每天早上都喝咖啡。"},{"ja":"明日、京都へ行きます。","en":"I'm going to Kyoto tomorrow.","cn":"我明天要去…4204 tokens truncated…做某事之前；也可表示事件之前或多久以前","meaningEn":"before (doing); before (an event); ago","rule":"动词辞书形 + 前に / 名词 + の + 前に","notes":"The verb before 前に is always in dictionary form, even when talking about the past. With a length of time there is no の: 3年前に (three years ago).","group":"时间","examples":[{"ja":"寝る前に歯をみがきます。","en":"I brush my teeth before going to bed.","cn":"睡觉前刷牙。"},{"ja":"授業の前にコーヒーを飲みます。","en":"I drink coffee before class.","cn":"上课前喝咖啡。"},{"ja":"3年前に日本へ来ました。","en":"I came to Japan three years ago.","cn":"我三年前来到日本。"}]},{"id":"ato-de","jp":"〜後で","meaning":"表示做完某事之后","meaningEn":"after (doing); after (an event)","rule":"动词た形 + 後で / 名词 + の + 後で","notes":"The verb before 後で is always in た-form, even for future plans. On its own, 後で means 'later'.","group":"时间","examples":[{"ja":"晩ご飯を食べた後で、散歩をします。","en":"I take a walk after eating dinner.","cn":"晚饭后我去散散步。"},{"ja":"仕事の後で、いっしょに飲みに行きませんか。","en":"Would you like to go for a drink after work?","cn":"我们下班后出去喝一杯怎么样？"},{"ja":"テストが終わった後で、友達と遊びました。","en":"After the test was over, I hung out with friends.","cn":"测试结束后，我和朋友一起玩。"}]},{"id":"nagara","jp":"〜ながら（同时）","meaning":"表示同时进行两个动作“一边……一边……”","meaningEn":"while (doing two actions at the same time)","rule":"动词ます形词干 + ながら","notes":"Both actions are done by the same person. The main action comes last: in A-ながら B, B is the main activity.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"音楽を聞きながら勉強します。","en":"I study while listening to music.","cn":"我边听音乐边学习。"},{"ja":"父はいつも新聞を読みながら朝ご飯を食べます。","en":"My father always eats breakfast while reading the newspaper.","cn":"我父亲总是在看报纸的时候吃早餐。"},{"ja":"コーヒーを飲みながら話しましょう。","en":"Let's talk over coffee.","cn":"我们喝杯咖啡聊聊吧。"}]},{"id":"ni-iku","jp":"〜に行く","meaning":"表示去某地做某事","meaningEn":"go (somewhere) to do","rule":"动词ます形词干 + に行く / 名词 + に行く","notes":"来る and 帰る work the same way: 遊びに来る. With する-nouns the noun can come directly: 買い物に行く, 散歩に行く.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"デパートへ服を買いに行きます。","en":"I'm going to the department store to buy clothes.","cn":"我要去百货商店买些衣服。"},{"ja":"週末、海へ泳ぎに行きました。","en":"I went to the beach to swim on the weekend.","cn":"我周末去海里游泳。"},{"ja":"友達がうちへ遊びに来ました。","en":"A friend came over to my place to hang out.","cn":"一位朋友来拜访我们。"}]},{"id":"ga-suki-ga-kirai","jp":"〜が好き / 〜が嫌い","meaning":"表示喜欢／讨厌……","meaningEn":"like; dislike","rule":"名词 + が好き / 名词 + が嫌い / 动词辞书形 + の + が好き","notes":"好き and 嫌い are な-adjectives, so the thing liked takes が, not を. 大好き and 大嫌い are stronger. 嫌い can sound blunt; あまり好きじゃない is softer.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"私は甘いものが好きです。","en":"I like sweet things.","cn":"我喜欢甜食。"},{"ja":"弟は野菜が嫌いです。","en":"My younger brother doesn't like vegetables.","cn":"我弟弟讨厌蔬菜。"},{"ja":"母は料理をするのが好きです。","en":"My mother likes cooking.","cn":"我妈妈喜欢做饭。"}]},{"id":"ga-jouzu-ga-heta","jp":"〜が上手 / 〜が下手","meaning":"表示擅长／不擅长……","meaningEn":"good at; bad at","rule":"名词 + が上手 / 名词 + が下手","notes":"Mostly used about other people; calling yourself 上手 can sound like bragging. Both are な-adjectives: 料理が上手な人.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"姉はピアノが上手です。","en":"My older sister is good at the piano.","cn":"我姐姐是一位优秀的钢琴家。"},{"ja":"私は歌が下手です。","en":"I'm bad at singing.","cn":"我不擅长唱歌。"},{"ja":"マイクさんは日本語が上手ですね。","en":"Mike, your Japanese is really good.","cn":"迈克擅长日语，不是吗？"}]},{"id":"ga-aru-ga-iru","jp":"〜がある / 〜がいる","meaning":"表示存在或拥有：ある用于物，いる用于人和动物","meaningEn":"there is; there are; have (ある for things, いる for people and animals)","rule":"名词 + がある / 名词 + がいる","notes":"ある is for things, plants and events; いる is for people and animals. Negatives: ない / いない (polite: ありません / いません).","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"公園に大きい木があります。","en":"There is a big tree in the park.","cn":"公园里有一棵大树。"},{"ja":"私は妹が一人います。","en":"I have one younger sister.","cn":"我有一个姐姐。"},{"ja":"明日、日本語のテストがあります。","en":"There's a Japanese test tomorrow.","cn":"我明天有日语考试。"}]},{"id":"kara-reason","jp":"〜から（原因）","meaning":"表示原因“因为……”","meaningEn":"because; since; so","rule":"句子 + から","notes":"The reason comes first: A から B (A, so B). Answer どうして with 〜からです. Nouns and な-adjectives need だ: 雨だから.","group":"原因","examples":[{"ja":"今日は寒いから、コートを着ます。","en":"It's cold today, so I'll wear a coat.","cn":"今天很冷，所以我要穿件外套。"},{"ja":"時間がありませんから、タクシーで行きましょう。","en":"We don't have time, so let's take a taxi.","cn":"我们没有太多时间，所以我们乘坐出租车吧。"},{"ja":"「どうして休みましたか。」「頭が痛かったからです。」","en":"\"Why were you absent?\" \"Because I had a headache.\"","cn":"“你为什么休息？”“因为我头痛。”"}]},{"id":"ga-but","jp":"〜が（转折）","meaning":"连接转折“但是……”","meaningEn":"but; although","rule":"句子 + が","notes":"Also used just to soften a request or lead into a topic: すみませんが…. A little more formal than けど (N4).","group":"助词","examples":[{"ja":"この店は安いですが、あまりおいしくないです。","en":"This restaurant is cheap, but the food isn't very good.","cn":"这家商店很便宜，但不是很好吃。"},{"ja":"日本語は難しいですが、おもしろいです。","en":"Japanese is difficult, but interesting.","cn":"日语很难，但很有趣。"},{"ja":"すみませんが、ちょっと静かにしてください。","en":"Excuse me, but please be a little quieter.","cn":"不好意思，请保持安静。"}]},{"id":"deshou","jp":"〜でしょう","meaning":"表示推测、委婉判断或征求确认“……吧”","meaningEn":"probably; I think; ..., right?","rule":"动词普通形 / い形容词 / な形容词 / 名词 + でしょう","notes":"Typical of weather forecasts. Said with rising intonation, it asks the listener to agree. Plain form: だろう (N4).","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"明日は雨が降るでしょう。","en":"It will probably rain tomorrow.","cn":"明天会下雨。"},{"ja":"山の上は寒いでしょう。","en":"It's probably cold at the top of the mountain.","cn":"山上会很冷。"},{"ja":"このかばん、かわいいでしょう？","en":"This bag is cute, isn't it?","cn":"这个包很可爱吧？"}]},{"id":"ku-naru-ni-naru","jp":"〜くなる / 〜になる","meaning":"表示变化“变得……”","meaningEn":"become; get; turn","rule":"い形容词く形 + なる / な形容词 + になる / 名词 + になる","notes":"いい becomes よくなる. Often used in the past to describe a change that has happened: 大きくなりました.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"あたたかくなりましたね。","en":"It's gotten warmer, hasn't it?","cn":"热身。"},{"ja":"部屋がきれいになりました。","en":"The room has become clean.","cn":"房间已打扫干净。"},{"ja":"兄は来年、医者になります。","en":"My older brother will become a doctor next year.","cn":"我哥哥明年就要当医生了。"}]},{"id":"ni-suru","jp":"〜にする（decide）","meaning":"表示决定或选择“决定要……”","meaningEn":"decide on; choose; I'll have","rule":"名词 + にする","notes":"Common when ordering food or picking from options. Past: 〜にしました (I decided on ...).","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"私はカレーにします。","en":"I'll have the curry.","cn":"我会做咖喱。"},{"ja":"飲み物は何にしますか。","en":"What would you like to drink?","cn":"您想喝什么？"},{"ja":"旅行は来月にしましょう。","en":"Let's plan the trip for next month.","cn":"下个月出行。"}]},{"id":"mada-te-inai","jp":"まだ〜ていない","meaning":"表示尚未发生“还没有……”","meaningEn":"not yet (have done)","rule":"まだ + 动词て形 + いない / まだ + 动词て形 + いません","notes":"Use ていない, not ませんでした, for something that may still happen. The short answer is いいえ、まだです.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"まだ昼ご飯を食べていません。","en":"I haven't eaten lunch yet.","cn":"我还没吃午饭呢。"},{"ja":"「宿題はもうしましたか。」「いいえ、まだしていません。」","en":"\"Have you done your homework yet?\" \"No, not yet.\"","cn":"“你的作业做完了吗？”“不，我没有。”"},{"ja":"電車はまだ来ていません。","en":"The train hasn't come yet.","cn":"火车还没有到。"}]},{"id":"mou-ta","jp":"もう〜た","meaning":"表示动作已经发生“已经……”","meaningEn":"already (have done); (in questions) yet","rule":"もう + 动词た形 / もう + 动词ます形词干 + ました","notes":"In questions もう means 'yet'. With a negative verb, もう means 'no longer': もう食べません.","group":"时间","examples":[{"ja":"「もう晩ご飯を食べましたか。」「はい、もう食べました。」","en":"\"Have you eaten dinner yet?\" \"Yes, I already have.\"","cn":"“你吃过晚饭了吗？”“是的，我已经吃过了。”"},{"ja":"妹はもう寝ました。","en":"My younger sister has already gone to bed.","cn":"我姐姐已经睡着了。"},{"ja":"映画はもう始まりましたよ。","en":"The movie has already started.","cn":"电影已经开始了。"}]},{"id":"amari-nai","jp":"あまり〜ない","meaning":"あまり＋否定：不太……","meaningEn":"not very; not much; not often","rule":"あまり + 动词ない形 / あまり + い形容词く形 + ない / あまり + な形容词 + じゃない","notes":"Always followed by a negative form. あまり好きじゃない is a softer way to say you dislike something.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"私はあまりテレビを見ません。","en":"I don't watch much TV.","cn":"我不看太多电视。"},{"ja":"このりんごはあまり甘くないです。","en":"This apple isn't very sweet.","cn":"这个苹果不是很甜。"},{"ja":"今日はあまり忙しくありません。","en":"I'm not very busy today.","cn":"我今天不太忙。"}]},{"id":"zenzen-nai","jp":"全然〜ない","meaning":"全然＋否定：完全不……","meaningEn":"not at all; not in the least","rule":"全然 + 动词ない形 / 全然 + い形容词く形 + ない / 全然 + な形容词 + じゃない","notes":"Stronger than あまり〜ない. In casual speech 全然 is sometimes used with positive words (全然大丈夫), but with a negative is the standard use.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"この問題は全然わかりません。","en":"I don't understand this question at all.","cn":"我对此问题一无所知。"},{"ja":"今日は全然寒くないです。","en":"It's not cold at all today.","cn":"今天一点也不冷。"},{"ja":"弟は全然勉強しません。","en":"My younger brother doesn't study at all.","cn":"我哥哥根本不学习。"}]},{"id":"dake","jp":"〜だけ","meaning":"限定范围“只／仅仅……”","meaningEn":"only; just","rule":"名词 + だけ / 动词辞书形 + だけ","notes":"Neutral in tone. Compare しか〜ない (N4), which stresses that the amount is small.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"財布に100円だけあります。","en":"I only have 100 yen in my wallet.","cn":"钱包里只有100日元。"},{"ja":"朝はコーヒーだけ飲みます。","en":"In the morning I only have coffee.","cn":"我只在早上喝咖啡。"},{"ja":"日曜日だけ休みです。","en":"Sunday is my only day off.","cn":"仅在周日休息。"}]},{"id":"kurai-gurai","jp":"〜くらい / 〜ぐらい（大约）","meaning":"表示大约的数量或时长“左右”","meaningEn":"about; approximately (an amount or length of time)","rule":"名词 + くらい / 名词 + ぐらい","notes":"Used with amounts and durations. For a point in time (around three o'clock), use ごろ: 3時ごろ.","group":"数量","examples":[{"ja":"駅まで歩いて10分ぐらいです。","en":"It's about a ten-minute walk to the station.","cn":"步行约10分钟即可抵达车站。"},{"ja":"毎日2時間くらい勉強します。","en":"I study for about two hours every day.","cn":"我每天学习大约2个小时。"},{"ja":"このかばんは5000円ぐらいでした。","en":"This bag was about 5,000 yen.","cn":"这个包的价格约为5000日元。"}]},{"id":"goro","jp":"〜ごろ","meaning":"表示大致的时间点“……左右”","meaningEn":"around; about (a point in time)","rule":"名词 + ごろ","notes":"Attaches to clock times, dates and months. に after ごろ is optional: 7時ごろ(に)起きます.","group":"时间","examples":[{"ja":"毎晩11時ごろ寝ます。","en":"I go to bed around eleven every night.","cn":"我每天晚上11点左右睡觉。"},{"ja":"4月ごろ、桜が咲きます。","en":"The cherry blossoms bloom around April.","cn":"樱花在四月左右盛开。"},{"ja":"夕方6時ごろに家に帰ります。","en":"I get home around six in the evening.","cn":"我会在下午6点左右回家。"}]},{"id":"nani-mo-nai-dare-mo-nai","jp":"何も〜ない / 誰も〜ない","meaning":"疑问词＋も＋否定：什么也不／谁也不","meaningEn":"nothing; nobody; not anything; not anyone","rule":"何も + 动词ない形 / 誰も + 动词ない形","notes":"With places, a particle comes before も: どこにも / どこへも行きません (go nowhere). 誰 is often written in hiragana: だれ.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"けさは何も食べませんでした。","en":"I didn't eat anything this morning.","cn":"我什么都没吃。"},{"ja":"教室にはだれもいません。","en":"There's nobody in the classroom.","cn":"教室里没有人。"},{"ja":"冷蔵庫の中には何もありません。","en":"There's nothing in the fridge.","cn":"冰箱里什么都没有。"}]},{"id":"nani-ka-dare-ka-doko-ka","jp":"何か / 誰か / どこか","meaning":"表示某个东西／某个人／某个地方","meaningEn":"something; someone; somewhere","rule":"疑问词 + か","notes":"Question word + か gives 'some-' words; question word + も + negative gives 'no-' words. が and を after 何か / だれか are often dropped.","group":"疑问","examples":[{"ja":"何か飲みますか。","en":"Would you like something to drink?","cn":"你想喝点什么吗？"},{"ja":"だれか来ましたよ。","en":"Someone's here.","cn":"有人来了。"},{"ja":"夏休みにどこかへ行きましたか。","en":"Did you go anywhere during summer vacation?","cn":"暑假期间您去过什么地方吗？"}]},{"id":"kore-sore-are-dore","jp":"これ / それ / あれ / どれ","meaning":"指示代词：这个／那个（你附近）／那个（远处）／哪一个","meaningEn":"this one; that one (near you); that one (over there); which one","rule":"これ / それ / あれ / どれ","notes":"こ = near the speaker, そ = near the listener, あ = away from both, ど = question. They stand alone; as a subject どれ takes が, not は.","group":"指示词","examples":[{"ja":"これは私の辞書です。","en":"This is my dictionary.","cn":"这是我的字典。"},{"ja":"それは何ですか。","en":"What is that?","cn":"是什么？"},{"ja":"「あなたのかさはどれですか。」「あれです。」","en":"\"Which one is your umbrella?\" \"That one over there.\"","cn":"“你的雨伞是什么？”“就是这样。”"}]},{"id":"kono-sono-ano-dono","jp":"この / その / あの / どの","meaning":"连体指示词：这个／那个／哪一个……","meaningEn":"this; that (near you); that ... over there; which (before a noun)","rule":"この / その / あの / どの + 名词","notes":"Always followed by a noun: この本, never この alone. これ / それ / あれ / どれ are used when there is no noun.","group":"指示词","examples":[{"ja":"このケーキはおいしいです。","en":"This cake is delicious.","cn":"这个蛋糕很好吃。"},{"ja":"その本はだれのですか。","en":"Whose book is that?","cn":"这是谁的书？"},{"ja":"「どの人が先生ですか。」「あの人です。」","en":"\"Which person is the teacher?\" \"That person over there.\"","cn":"“老师是谁？”“就是他。”"}]},{"id":"koko-soko-asoko-doko","jp":"ここ / そこ / あそこ / どこ","meaning":"表示地点：这里／那里（你附近）／那里／哪里","meaningEn":"here; there (near you); over there; where","rule":"ここ / そこ / あそこ / どこ","notes":"こちら / そちら / あちら / どちら are politer versions: お国はどちらですか (Where are you from?).","group":"指示词","examples":[{"ja":"ここは私の学校です。","en":"This is my school.","cn":"这是我的学校。"},{"ja":"トイレはあそこです。","en":"The restroom is over there.","cn":"厕所在那边。"},{"ja":"すみません、駅はどこですか。","en":"Excuse me, where is the station?","cn":"对不起，车站在哪里？"}]},{"id":"ku-nai-katta-ku-nakatta","jp":"〜くない / 〜かった / 〜くなかった","meaning":"い形容词的否定、过去和过去否定变化","meaningEn":"negative and past forms of i-adjectives (is not; was; was not)","rule":"い形容词 stem + くない / い形容词 stem + かった / い形容词 stem + くなかった","notes":"高い→高くない, 高かった, 高くなかった. Add です to be polite. いい is irregular: よくない, よかった, よくなかった.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"この部屋はあまり広くないです。","en":"This room isn't very big.","cn":"这个房间不是很大。"},{"ja":"きのうのテストは難しかったです。","en":"Yesterday's test was difficult.","cn":"昨天的考试很难。"},{"ja":"先週見た映画はおもしろくなかったです。","en":"The movie I saw last week wasn't interesting.","cn":"我上周看的电影不太有趣。"}]},{"id":"na-na-adjective","jp":"〜な（な形容词）","meaning":"な形容词修饰名词时用な，句末接です／だ","meaningEn":"na-adjectives: take な before a noun and です or だ at the end of a sentence","rule":"な形容词 + な + 名词 / な形容词 + です / な形容词 + ではありません / な形容词 + でした","notes":"Before a noun, add な: 静かな部屋. At the end of a sentence they change like nouns. きれい and きらい end in い but are な-adjectives.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"京都は有名な町です。","en":"Kyoto is a famous city.","cn":"京都是一个著名的小镇。"},{"ja":"きのうは暇でした。","en":"I was free yesterday.","cn":"昨天我有空。"},{"ja":"この部屋はあまり静かではありません。","en":"This room isn't very quiet.","cn":"这个房间不是很安静。"}]},{"id":"kute-de","jp":"〜くて / 〜で","meaning":"连接形容词或名词“……而且……”","meaningEn":"and (linking adjectives or nouns)","rule":"い形容词く形 + て / な形容词 + で / 名词 + で","notes":"いい becomes よくて. Join qualities that point the same way (both good or both bad); for a contrast, use が instead.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"この店は安くておいしいです。","en":"This restaurant is cheap and good.","cn":"这家商店物美价廉。"},{"ja":"私の町は静かできれいです。","en":"My town is quiet and clean.","cn":"我的小镇安静干净。"},{"ja":"兄は大学生で、妹は高校生です。","en":"My older brother is a university student, and my younger sister is a high school student.","cn":"我哥哥是大学生，我姐姐是高中生。"}]},{"id":"to-iu-named","jp":"〜という（命名）","meaning":"表示名称“叫作……”","meaningEn":"called; named","rule":"名词 + という + 名词","notes":"Introduces a name the listener may not know.","group":"句型","examples":[{"ja":"これは「すきやき」という料理です。","en":"This is a dish called sukiyaki.","cn":"这是一道名为「sukiyaki」的菜。"},{"ja":"「さくら」という店でアルバイトをしています。","en":"I work part-time at a shop called Sakura.","cn":"我在一家名为「SAKURA」的商店兼职工作。"},{"ja":"山田さんという人から電話がありました。","en":"There was a call from someone named Yamada.","cn":"我接到一个叫山田先生的电话。"}]}]
